# explainer-tab (M11): what ? opened closes as Tab takes the focus out of the row: k's box clicked,
# Shift+Tab back to it, ? (explainer-key), Tab. The next stop is b's flip toggle in Chromium and the
# port (plan call 3 f; WebKit's plain Tab goes to b's box), so judged against Chromium's shots; the
# explainer closes in every engine. Shift+Tab within a row (from k's box) would keep it. Inputs and
# closing shots fall on the 16 ms grid: a closing explainer is gone at its exit's end, React's at
# that instant, the port's from its next frame. ? is pressed with Shift held, as a US keyboard sends
# it: React sees the key ?, SDL hands the port / with Shift (SDL 3's key events carry the key
# unshifted); Playwright's ? alone has no Shift, and Shift+/ reaches the page as /.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 2000
click 383 468
wait 16
tab shift
wait 16
hold Shift
key ?
release Shift
wait 1104
tab
shot tab-0000
wait 208
shot tab-gone
